+---
+title: 'pp-funfix-118-124 — kill the era-3 death clock, give the meter a way back'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-09-01'
+status: 'in-progress'
+baseline_commit: '61ea014de2726ceabf46c015ebd0e6a4254e837a'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: ['project-context.md']
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** (#118) era-3's arrival starts an unwinnable death clock — the playtest squad measured every strategy run dead 16.7–28.4 s after the era flip (first meter dip 41.9–42.6 s, dead 46.8–47.5 s), before the marquee surge even opens at 60 s; the drain evidence (first dip → death ≈ 5.0 s at ~1%/tick) pins the killer as the EMAIL grace expiring (breached since era 2 on a grown standard mesh), with streaming's clock right behind it. (#124) the meter heals only when NO class is breach-latched — in observed play it is a one-way drain: any post-grace breach empties it in 2.5–5 s.
+
+**Approach:** Pure balance + one small mechanic, per the issues' "tunables, not a rewrite". #118: extend BOTH classes' `health_grace_ticks` 400 → 900 (45 s — covers the fiber-sprint window; the fiber spool only exists from era 3's box grant, so pre-arrival conversion is impossible — the grace IS the counterplay window). #124: add the issue's streak-gated meter refill — after `meter_refill_streak_ticks` (200) ticks with NO active drain, the meter refills at `meter_refill_per_tick` (1%/tick) even while classes remain breach-latched-in-grace; the existing all-clear recharge is untouched.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:** integer-only sim math (ODN-10); balance numbers single-sourced in data/*.json (ODN-5); breach thresholds, drain rates, drain cap, grace-refill guard, tolerances, win condition (surge 90) all UNCHANGED — a never-converting player still dies (post-grace drain → empty → Run_Lost); new behavior pinned by core tests with measured tick values (never guessed); golden shifts re-blessed only via the sanctioned rlsw pipeline (`harness save` + `harness input-parity save` + replay gate + `tools/ci-local.sh --mac`).
+
+**Ask First:** if the survivable golden cannot be produced with grace 900 + prompt wide conversion (i.e. the arrival is still unsurvivable), HALT — that means the ramp lever (issue option 1) is also needed and the scope grows.
+
+**Never:** no new systems (no repair action, no Box-economy coupling — the issue's smaller proposal wins); no demand-volume or credit-gate changes; no SLA tolerance/exit-margin moves; no serialization/LOG_VERSION changes (the streak scratch is derived, never serialized); no lose-state softening beyond the grace window (post-grace drain stays lethal — #115 must not regress); do not touch #119's era-forecast surface (separate issue).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Prepared ride (#118) | era-2 mesh, gate fires era 3 @30 s, wide conversion within ~5 s | breach may latch but exits within the 900-tick grace — zero drain ticks; run survives into the surge window | N/A |
+| Ignored arrival | era-3 breach, no conversion | first drain at breach+900 ticks (≈45 s later than today), then the unchanged 2–5 s drain to Run_Lost | E17 unchanged |
+| Streak refill (#124) | classes breach-latched-in-grace, no post-grace drain for 200 ticks | meter +1%/tick (Meter_Changed emits), capped at 100 | N/A |
+| Active drain | any class post-grace breached | refill blocked; streak reset to 0 every drain tick; drain semantics byte-identical to today | E16 unchanged |
+| All-clear | no class breached | existing recharge_pct_per_tick path, unchanged | N/A |
+| Health disabled | `health on` absent | meter inert; new streak never gates anything observable | back-compat |
+| Catalog | missing new balance keys | fail-fast load error (jint -1 sentinel pattern) | loader rejects |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `core/health.odin` -- the meter: drain (E16), grace lifecycle (E30), recharge branch (the `else if !any_breach` arm — extend here); file header documents the contract — update it.
+- `core/types.odin:361` -- `Health_State`; add `no_drain_streak: u32` next to `prev_in_surge` (derived scratch — never serialized, not in the T1 hash, like prev_*).
+- `core/catalog.odin:372,1104,1125` -- `Health_Balance` struct + fail-fast parse/validate; add `meter_refill_per_tick` (>= 1) + `meter_refill_streak_ticks` (>= 1) mirroring the grace_refill pair.
+- `data/balance.json` -- `health` block: the two new knobs + `_comment` update (rationale: the #124 issue proposal, integer-grid adaptation).
+- `data/packet_types.json` -- both entries `health_grace_ticks` 400 → 900 + `_comment` update (rationale: the modernize-sprint window; fiber spool is era-3-gated).
+- `core/health_test.odin` -- the durable pins; grace-dependent exact-tick pins re-derive from measured runs; NEW test pins the streak refill (heals in-grace, blocked by active drain, streak reset).
+- `demos/health_win.dem`, `demos/health_lose.dem` -- the story-4.3 goldens: lose timings shift (grace 900), win is catalog-hash-only; refresh the lose captures to the measured ticks.
