+- `demos/health_recover.dem` (NEW) -- the #124 golden: narrow-path saturation → Grace_Expired → meter mid-drain → demolish+wide-fan fix → breach exits → meter refills to 100; capture the trough and the full recovery.
+- `tools/harness.sh` -- `run | save | replay`; the rlsw re-bless entry point.
+- `harness/stats.odin` -- the stats stream (evidence for the tuning table); `--stats-out` per-tick CSVs.
+- `_pr_body_pace.md` -- the prior balance-change PR: the re-bless ritual + tuning-table format to mirror.
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- [x] `data/packet_types.json` + `data/balance.json` -- the tuning move (both graces 900; two new health knobs) + comments -- the whole fix is these four numbers plus the refill mechanic.
+- [x] `core/types.odin` + `core/catalog.odin` -- the streak scratch field + the two validated knobs -- ODN-5/ODN-10 compliance.
+- [x] `core/health.odin` -- streak update in the drain/recharge branch + the in-grace refill arm + header docs -- the #124 mechanic.
+- [x] `core/health_test.odin` -- re-pin grace-shifted tests from measured runs + the new streak-refill test -- acceptance = durable tests, not PR prose.
+- [x] `demos/era3_surge_survivable.dem` + `demos/health_recover.dem` -- author, run, READ the stats, write the measured-number headers, bless -- the acceptance goldens.
+- [x] `demos/health_lose.dem` (+ any other shifted captures) -- re-time captures to measured ticks -- honest goldens.
+- [x] full corpus re-bless -- `tools/harness.sh save` + `harness input-parity save` + replay verify + `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` -- sanctioned rlsw pipeline.
+- [x] repro the death clock pre/post on a fun-run-shaped mesh with `--stats-out` -- the tuning table's before/after numbers.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given the era-3 arrival on a prepared (promptly-modernized) mesh, when the gate fires era 3, then zero drain ticks occur and the run carries the surge with meter > 0 (the era3_surge_survivable golden).
+- Given a run whose meter has drained below 100, when the network stops actively draining for 200+ ticks, then the meter refills at 1%/tick and the health_recover golden shows trough → full recovery.
+- Given a never-converting player, when the grace expires with the breach live, then Run_Lost still fires on the unchanged drain (tension preserved; #115 not regressed).
+- Given the whole corpus re-blessed, when `tools/harness.sh run` + `odin test core` + `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` run, then all green.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+The evidence re-derivation that shaped the fix (carry to the PR): first dip 41.9–42.6 s with era 3 at 30.1 s means the latched class breached ~12 s BEFORE the flip — email, in era 2 (500‰ legacy decay on a grown standard mesh pushes the windowed avg latency over 2000 ms); 5.0 s of 1%/tick drain to death = email's severity, alone (streaming's grace ran to ~50.2 s, never reached). So a streaming-only grace extension (the issue's literal example) would NOT have saved the observed runs — both classes need the sprint window. Streaming keeps its own 900 for its era-3 clock (its breach latches at the flip; 45 s covers conversion + the 200-tick window slide).
+
+Streak semantics: `no_drain_streak` counts ticks where the E16 drain computed 0 (both in the breach-in-grace case and the all-clear case); ANY drain tick resets it to 0. The new refill arm fires only when `!any_breach` is false (the all-clear arm keeps the existing faster path) AND the streak >= `meter_refill_streak_ticks` AND meter < 100. The issue suggested 0.25%/tick; the integer grid (ODN-10 + the u8 Meter_Changed payload) admits 1%/tick — document the adaptation in the PR (recovery remains 4× slower than death's max drain, and only while no drain is active).
+
+Tension preservation (#115): the lose state's reach is UNCHANGED in structure — neglect through the (now 45 s) grace still ends in the unchanged 2–5 s terminal drain; refill requires zero active drain for 10 s, unreachable while dying; win condition untouched. The #115 complaint (lose unreachable in short/no-service play) lives in paths this job never touches.
+
+## Verification
