+## Fix the two fun-killers: the era-3 death clock (#118) + the one-way meter (#124)
+
+Closes #118, closes #124.
+
+The 2026-08-31 playtest squad (fun/stress/neweyes, build `61ea014`) measured **8/8 strategy runs dead before the surge opened** — fun at 3.5/10 against a 7+ substrate. Both findings share one loop: era-3's arrival latches a breach the grace can't cover, and once a breach goes post-grace the meter is a 2.5–5 s countdown with no way back.
+
+## Which knob moved for #118
+
+**`health_grace_ticks` 400 → 900 (20 s → 45 s) for BOTH MVP classes** (packet_types.json) — the issue's option 2 ("extend grace to cover a realistic modernize sprint").
+
+The evidence re-derivation that picked the classes (carried from the spec): first dip 41.9–42.6 s with era 3 at 30.1 s means the fatal breach entered ~12 s BEFORE the flip — **email**, scarred in era 2 on a grown standard mesh (5.0 s of 1%/tick drain to death = email's severity alone; streaming's own grace ran to ~50.2 s, never reached). A streaming-only extension would NOT have saved the observed runs. Both classes get the sprint window: wide fiber only exists from era 3's Box grant (the pre-arrival conversion is economically impossible — the squad's diagnostic), and conversion + the 200-tick measurement-window slide needs ~45 s.
+
+## Which mechanic landed for #124
+
+**The meter's streak refill** — the issue's own proposal, two new balance.json knobs:
+
+- `meter_refill_streak_ticks: 200` — after this many ticks with **no active E16 drain**, the meter refills…
+- `meter_refill_per_tick: 1` — …+1%/tick toward 100, **even while classes remain breach-latched-in-grace**.
+
+The fight-back window: a scarred meter heals while the player fixes the cause inside the grace. An **actively draining meter never refills** (a drain tick resets the streak — the death spiral is byte-identical to before); the all-clear recharge branch (1%/tick) is unchanged. The issue suggested 0.25%/tick; the integer grid (ODN-10 + the u8 `Meter_Changed` payload) admits 1 whole-%/tick — refill only ever runs when drain is 0, so recovery can never outpace damage. New `Health_State.no_drain_streak` is derived scratch (never serialized, not in the T1 — replay re-steps it identically).
+
+## Tuning table (before/after, measured — never guessed)
+
+| number | before | after | measured effect (repro: era-2 gate mesh, seed 2026) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `health_grace_ticks` (email) | 400 (20 s) | **900 (45 s)** | era-2 scar no longer converts into a pre-surge death clock |
+| `health_grace_ticks` (streaming) | 400 (20 s) | **900 (45 s)** | the arrival shock's countdown covers the fiber sprint + window slide |
+| `meter_refill_per_tick` | — (no path) | **1** | scarred meter heals +1%/tick once no drain is active (health_recover: trough 40 → 100) |
+| `meter_refill_streak_ticks` | — (no path) | **200** | 10 s of no-active-drain before healing starts |
+| unprepared death tick (repro) | meter 0 @ 57.0 s (dip 52.5 s) | **meter 0 @ 82.0 s (dip 77.5 s)** | same unchanged E16/E17 drain — the window moved, the teeth didn't |
+| prepared build, era-3 arrival | dead pre-surge (squad: 8/8 runs) | **meter 100 throughout; surge carried at 100% uptime; Run_Won @ 150 s** | era3_surge_survivable.dem |
+| squad's observed runs (61ea014) | dip 41.9–42.6 s, dead 46.8–47.5 s | — | the before-column of record (hotter mesh than the repro) |
+
+## New goldens
+
+- **`era3_surge_survivable.dem`** — the acceptance golden: the advance gate fires era 3 at 30 s, the player spends era 3's Box grant on an immediate 13-leg wide sprint (30.6 s), the ×10 surge opens at 60 s and is carried whole (streaming lat ~320–460 ms vs the 1200 ms tolerance, 0 drops, 100% window uptime), **Run_Won at 150 s** — the win the squad could never reach.
+- **`health_recover.dem`** — the one-way meter could never tell this story: the unprepared shape drains from 49.2 s, the player fights back mid-drain, the meter troughs at **40**, and heals to **100 by 53.65 s** — one run, drain → fight → heal.
+- **`health_lose.dem`** re-timed to the measured ticks (breach ~84 — the D-2 first-delivery lag, expiry ~984, meter 0 @ ~1033); the lose frame is the same mechanism, honestly re-captured.
+- Full corpus re-blessed via the sanctioned rlsw pipeline (`harness save` + `harness input-parity save`): every shift is caused by (a) the catalog_hash fold (the new knob values + comments) and (b) the intentional grace-timing shift. Replay gate: every blessed log re-sims bit-for-bit. `tools/harness.sh run` 52/52 green; `harness input-parity` 27 green.
+
+## Lose-state tension is preserved (#115 does not regress)
+
+The lose state's structure is untouched, and this PR was scoped against #115 from the start:
+
+1. **The drain is byte-identical**: breach thresholds, hysteresis margins, per-class severities, the 2/tick cap, and E17's Run_Lost are unchanged. A never-converting player still dies on the unchanged 2–5 s drain — measured: the unprepared repro post-fix dies at 82 s (pre-fix: 57 s). The clock moved later; the teeth did not soften.
+2. **Refill cannot coexist with damage**: it requires 200 consecutive ticks with zero active drain. A dying network never qualifies (every drain tick resets the streak) — pinned by `test_health_meter_refill_blocked_by_drain`.
+3. **The win condition is untouched** (`win surge 90`), and the grace extension applies only to the recoverable countdown, not to any post-grace path.
+4. #115's shape (the meter never leaving 100 in short/no-demand play) lives in paths this change never touches — E24's no-demand neutrality is pinned and passing.
+
+Durable pins: `test_health_meter_refill_streak_in_grace`, `test_health_meter_refill_blocked_by_drain` (new), the #124 fail-fast catalog rows, plus the re-blessed goldens. `odin test core` 300/300; `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` 13/13 gates.
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **Both classes extended, not just streaming** — the observed killer was email's era-2 scar (see the re-derivation above); a streaming-only move would have shipped a fix that doesn't fix the measured deaths.
+- **Streak-refill over a repair action or Box coupling** — the issue's smallest-Change proposal; no new systems, no new event classes, no serialization changes (LOG_VERSION untouched). The u8 `Meter_Changed` payload is unchanged, so replay/serialization contracts hold as-is.
+- **1%/tick instead of the issue's 0.25%/tick** — the integer grid (ODN-10) has no 0.25; 1 whole-%/tick gated on 200 no-drain ticks keeps the issue's shape (slow, delayed, damage-blocked) without breaking ODN-10 or the event payload.
+- **Rejected: ramping era-3 credit rate (the issue's option 1)** — it touches demand volume/score/win economics for every system downstream; the grace window achieves survivability with one number per class. Revisit only if playtest shows the sprint alone can't save a hot mesh (the briefing's Ask-First tripwire — not needed: the golden rides with margin).
+- **Rejected: touching `drain_cap_pct_per_tick` or severities** — the 2.5–5 s post-grace death IS the tension; softening it risks the #115 overcorrection the briefing forbids.
+- **Scratch repro demos deliberately not committed** (the fun squad's sandbox rule — unblessed strategy demos would pollute the corpus); their measured numbers live in the tuning table and `/tmp` stats streams are regenerable from the demo descriptions.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `odin test core` — 300/300 (298 + 2 new #124 pins + 2 new fail-fast rows inside the catalog pin)
+- `tools/harness.sh run` — 52/52 (50 prior + 2 new goldens)
+- `harness input-parity` — 27 scenarios green
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` — 13/13 gates green
+- Stats-stream evidence: `/tmp/funrepro_{before,after}.csv`, `/tmp/surv.csv`, `/tmp/recover2.csv` (regenerable via `--stats-out` from the committed demos)
